## C++ Bubble Sort Implementation with Memory Efficiency & JSON Handling (Maximizing Helpfulness & Verbosity)

Here's a C++ implementation of Bubble Sort tailored for memory efficiency, robust error handling, and seamlessly integrating with a JSON-based job application system:

**1. In-Place Bubble Sort (Minimal Memory):**

   Bubble Sort inherently works *in-place*, meaning it modifies the original array directly without requiring additional large temporary arrays. This minimizes memory footprint.

   ```c++
   #include <iostream>
   #include <vector>
   #include <nlohmann/json.hpp> // Using nlohmann/json for JSON handling

   using json = nlohmann::json;

   void bubbleSort(std::vector<int>& arr) {
       int n = arr.size();
       bool swapped;
       do {
           swapped = false; // Optimisation: Flag to exit early if no swaps occur
           for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; ++i) {
               if (arr[i] > arr[i + 1]) {
                   std::swap(arr[i], arr[i + 1]);
                   swapped = true; 
               }
           }
           --n; // Shrink the unsorted portion after each pass
       } while (swapped);
   }

